' F14 -- Trust boundaries and RLS policy patterns.
' Chapter 5 (Implementation). Concept diagram.
' Claim supported: authorisation has two enforcement points. RLS bounds direct
' client access (68 tables, all RLS-enabled, four policy patterns, UNION
' semantics as the structural hazard). The FastAPI backend mostly runs as
' service_role or over asyncpg, bypasses RLS, and checks ownership in Python.
@startuml f14-trust-boundaries
!include _style.iuml

title Trust boundaries — two enforcement points

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**UNTRUSTED**" as UT #DCDCDC {
  rectangle "Browser\nholds the anon key,\nbaked into the bundle" as BR
  rectangle "Uploaded PDF text\nprofessor OR student" as PDF #DCDCDC
}

rectangle "**Identity boundary**" as ID #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Supabase Auth\nJWT issuer" as JWT
  rectangle "anon\nno claims" as ANON
  rectangle "authenticated\nauth.uid() present" as AUTH
  rectangle "service_role\nbypasses RLS entirely" as SR #BFBFBF
}

rectangle "**Postgres RLS — the boundary for direct client access**\n68 tables, every one RLS-enabled" as RLS #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "**P1 Owner-scoped**\nuser_id = auth.uid()\nxp_events, review_schedule,\nexam_attempts, notifications" as P1
  rectangle "**P2 Role-gated ownership**\nowner = uid AND has_role(professor)\ncourses, lectures" as P2
  rectangle "**P3 Enrollment-derived**\nEXISTS join via course_enrollments\nor assignment_lectures\nslides, quiz_questions, review_cards" as P3
  rectangle "**P4 Backend-only**\nno anon/authenticated policy at all\nparse_runs, slide_embeddings, caches" as P4 #DCDCDC
}

rectangle "**FastAPI — the boundary for backend paths**\nservice_role client + asyncpg pool,\nboth bypass RLS; ownership checked in Python" as API #F2F2F2

BR --> JWT
JWT --> ANON
JWT --> AUTH
ANON -[#1A1A1A,dashed]-> RLS : "**zero** table policies\ngrant TO anon"
AUTH --> P1
AUTH --> P2
AUTH --> P3
BR --> API
API --> SR
SR --> P4
PDF -[#1A1A1A,dashed]-> P3 : "content flows into\nanother user's\ntutor context"

note bottom of RLS
  **The structural hazard.** Postgres OR-combines permissive
  SELECT policies, so effective visibility is the UNION of every
  applicable policy — not the intersection. Called out explicitly
  in migration 20260719020000:25-29.

  **And it is untested end to end:** no test composes a real
  endpoint against real RLS (MILESTONE_2026_08.md:205-210), so the
  union behaviour that caused the original cross-tenant leak
  remains unguarded at the integration level.
end note

note right of P4
  service_role bypasses RLS, so
  every P4 table is protected only
  by the API's own checks. This is
  why lecture ownership is verified
  in chat_service before retrieval
  (see F12) — the database will not
  do it for this path.
end note

legend bottom
  Browser-to-PostgREST traffic is bounded by RLS. Most backend traffic is not: it runs as
  service_role or over asyncpg, so a missing ownership check there is invisible to the
  database. See F15 for how the policies were hardened, F4 for why uploads are untrusted.
endlegend

@enduml
